1:["$","main",null,{"className":"site article-page","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"article-frame","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"desktop-brand","href":"/","children":"Thinkinghaus"}],["$","article",null,{"className":"article-column","children":[["$","header",null,{"className":"article-header","children":[["$","h1",null,{"children":"An odyssey"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"August 6, 2026"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"3 minutes"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"article-body","children":[[["$","p","0-There’s an early scene in Christopher Nolan’s *The Odyssey* where Odysseus is sitting with Eumaeus, examining a litter of puppies. Eumaeus picks one up, looks it over briefly, and casually tosses it over a nearby ledge.",{"children":["There’s an early scene in Christopher Nolan’s ",["$","em","1",{"children":"The Odyssey"}]," where Odysseus is sitting with Eumaeus, examining a litter of puppies. Eumaeus picks one up, looks it over briefly, and casually tosses it over a nearby ledge."]}],["$","p","1-For a moment, the movie opens onto a stranger world. People live closer to death. The borders between necessity, ritual, cruelty, and ordinary life aren’t where I expect them to be. Nobody stops to explain the rules.",{"children":["For a moment, the movie opens onto a stranger world. People live closer to death. The borders between necessity, ritual, cruelty, and ordinary life aren’t where I expect them to be. Nobody stops to explain the rules."]}],["$","p","2-Then Eumaeus reaches for another puppy. Odysseus stops him and keeps the dog for himself.",{"children":["Then Eumaeus reaches for another puppy. Odysseus stops him and keeps the dog for himself."]}],["$","p","3-And just like that I know where I am again.",{"children":["And just like that I know where I am again."]}],["$","p","4-I know who I’m supposed to identify with. I know who has behaved badly. Odysseus has demonstrated a recognizably modern kind of mercy, and the little door into that other world swings mostly shut.",{"children":["I know who I’m supposed to identify with. I know who has behaved badly. Odysseus has demonstrated a recognizably modern kind of mercy, and the little door into that other world swings mostly shut."]}],["$","p","5-I wanted the movie to leave it open a little longer.",{"children":["I wanted the movie to leave it open a little longer."]}],["$","p","6-I do this kind of translation myself all the time. A god becomes a psychological condition. A monster becomes trauma. A voyage becomes a metaphor for recovering from war. These interpretations can be useful; sometimes they’re exactly what gives me a way into an old story.",{"children":["I do this kind of translation myself all the time. A god becomes a psychological condition. A monster becomes trauma. A voyage becomes a metaphor for recovering from war. These interpretations can be useful; sometimes they’re exactly what gives me a way into an old story."]}],["$","p","7-But they can also make the old story suspiciously good at agreeing with me.",{"children":["But they can also make the old story suspiciously good at agreeing with me."]}],["$","p","8-Homer’s gods aren’t especially cooperative about this. They’re vain, generous, jealous, horny, petty, helpful, vindictive, terrifying. They don’t always behave like symbols for something more respectable. For most of human history, people lived with forces they couldn’t control and didn’t expect the universe to be fair, legible, or particularly interested in explaining itself.",{"children":"$La"}],"$Lb","$Lc","$Ld","$Le","$Lf","$L10"],null]}],"$L11"]}]]}]}]
a:["Homer’s gods aren’t especially cooperative about this. They’re vain, generous, jealous, horny, petty, helpful, vindictive, terrifying. They don’t always behave like symbols for something more respectable. For most of human history, people lived with forces they couldn’t control and didn’t expect the universe to be fair, legible, or particularly interested in explaining itself."]
b:["$","p","9-I’m not sure I’d enjoy living in that world. I’m also not sure I want it renovated before I get there.",{"children":["I’m not sure I’d enjoy living in that world. I’m also not sure I want it renovated before I get there."]}]
c:["$","p","10-There’s something valuable in allowing an old thing to remain old for a while—letting its assumptions sit beside mine without immediately deciding which familiar modern category they belong in. Not because the past was wiser. Plenty of it was awful. And strangeness isn’t automatically profound.",{"children":["There’s something valuable in allowing an old thing to remain old for a while—letting its assumptions sit beside mine without immediately deciding which familiar modern category they belong in. Not because the past was wiser. Plenty of it was awful. And strangeness isn’t automatically profound."]}]
d:["$","p","11-I just want the chance to meet it before I translate it.",{"children":["I just want the chance to meet it before I translate it."]}]
e:["$","p","12-That’s what I liked about the puppy scene. For a few uncomfortable seconds, I didn’t quite know how to understand what I was seeing. I’d have liked another beat of that.",{"children":["That’s what I liked about the puppy scene. For a few uncomfortable seconds, I didn’t quite know how to understand what I was seeing. I’d have liked another beat of that."]}]
f:["$","p","13-Let the gods remain gods for a minute.",{"children":["Let the gods remain gods for a minute."]}]
10:["$","p","14-Let the sea remain the sea.",{"children":["Let the sea remain the sea."]}]
11:["$","footer",null,{"className":"footer","children":[["$","a",null,{"className":"footer-brand","href":"/","children":"Thinkinghaus"}],["$","nav",null,{"className":"footer-links","aria-label":"Site","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"/about.html","children":"About"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"/links.html","children":"Links"}]]}]]}]
